SkyRC Charger for Home Assistant

The MIT license in LICENSE covers the original work in this repository by
Thibault PECH and contributors.

This repository started as a fork of jperquin/ha-skyrc-mc3000
(https://github.com/jperquin/ha-skyrc-mc3000), which published no license.
None of that project's code is left, apart from the calls to Home Assistant's
own APIs that any integration makes: the MC3000 support was removed, and the
integration (config flow, coordinator, entities, services) and the MC5000
driver were rewritten from the protocol of the official SkyRC app and Home
Assistant's own conventions. The MIT license covers the whole repository.

The icon and logo (icon.png and custom_components/skyrc_charger/brand/) are
the SkyRC app icon, taken from the official SkyRC app. The SkyRC name and
logo are trademarks of SkyRC Technology Co., Ltd.; LICENSE does not cover
them, and they are used here only to identify the chargers this
integration works with.
